Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8

Dear Gordon Lisle,

We have completed our review of the API 570 2nd edition released in October 1998. Following an assessment of the updated requirements against our current site rules for corrosion rate calculations and remaining life, the Inspection Department has determined that no adjustments are necessary for the ATU-100.

The existing inspection frequencies and CML locations defined in QSCP-IP-ATU100 Rev 0 remain technically sound and compliant with the new edition. We will continue to manage the Amine Treating Unit piping under the established class-based maxima of 5 and 10 years as originally specified.

Regards,  Douglas Ferreira

Douglas Ferreira, Inspection Supervisor, API 570 inspector, QSCP Hamilton Inspection Department